Jobsmith
========

Jobsmith is a fork of career-ops, extended with a full local web portal, a
GitHub Actions job scanner, and a sandbox harness for verification.

Upstream work
-------------

The substantial majority of this codebase is the work of
Santiago Fernández de Valderrama (https://santifer.io), released as career-ops
under the MIT License:

    https://github.com/santifer/career-ops
    Copyright (c) 2026 Santiago Fernández de Valderrama

That includes, and is not limited to:

  - the portal scanner and its 75+ ATS/job-board provider modules
  - the A–G evaluation methodology, including the Block G posting-legitimacy
    and ghost-job analysis
  - every mode prompt under modes/ (evaluation, tailoring, cover letters,
    interview suite, offer preparation, and the market-specific mode sets)
  - the CV/cover-letter generation pipeline and its fact-check gate
    (verify-cv-facts.mjs)
  - the tracker, its integrity tooling, and the analytics scripts
  - the Go terminal dashboard and the initial Next.js web application

